  mt=4, 51-68, 91 Inelastic scattering                            9437 1451   96
     The direct component was calculated with coupled channel code9437 1451   97
     ecis /19/.  Eight states, marked with an asterisk in the     9437 1451   98
     level scheme given below, of the ground state rotational band9437 1451   99
     were coupled in the calculation. Deformed optical potential  9437 1451  100
     parameters with a derivative woods-saxon absorption term were9437 1451  101
     taken from ref./20/:                                         9437 1451  102
        V    =46.2 - 0.3*En        (MeV)                          9437 1451  103
        Wv   =-1.2 + 0.15*En       (MeV),   En > 8 MeV            9437 1451  104
        Ws   = 3.6 + 0.4*En        (MeV),   En < 7 MeV            9437 1451  105
               6.4 + 0.1*(En-7)    (MeV),   En > 7 MeV            9437 1451  106
        Vso  = 6.2                 (mev)                          9437 1451  107
        r: rv = 1.26 ,  rs= 1.24    rso= 1.12 (fm)                9437 1451  108
        a: av = 0.615,  as= 0.50 ,  aso= 0.47 (fm)                9437 1451  109
        beta-2= 0.21,  beta-4= 0.065                              9437 1451  110
     The compound component was calculated with optical and       9437 1451  111
     statistical model code casthy /21/, taking into account      9437 1451  112
     level fluctuation and interference effects. The fission,     9437 1451  113
     (n,2n), (n,3n), and (n,4n) reactions were considered as      9437 1451  114
     competing processes.                                         9437 1451  115
                                                                  9437 1451  116
     The neutron transmission coefficients for the incident       9437 1451  117
     channel were generated with ecis, whereas those for the exit 9437 1451  118
     channel were calculated with casthy using spherical optical  9437 1451  119
     potential parameters adopted for JENDL-2 evaluation:         9437 1451  120
        V  = 40.72 - 0.05*En      (MeV)                           9437 1451  121
        Ws = 6.78 - 0.29*En       (MeV)                           9437 1451  122
        Vso= 7.0                  (MeV)                           9437 1451  123
        r  = rso= 1.32, rs =1.357 (fm)                            9437 1451  124
        a  = aso= b = 0.47        (fm)                            9437 1451  125
     The surface absorption is of derivative Woods-Saxon type.    9437 1451  126
     The level scheme was taken from ref./22/:                    9437 1451  127
