  mt= 16, 17, 37   (n,2n), (n,3n), and (n,4n)                     9437 1451  151
     Calculated with a modified version of gnash /23/.  The       9437 1451  152
     neutron transmission coefficients were generated with ecis   9437 1451  153
     /19/ and optical model code eliese-3 /24/, respectively,     9437 1451  154
     using the above-mentioned deformed and spherical potentials. 9437 1451  155
     The level schemes for pu-236, -237, -238, -239 and -240 were 9437 1451  156
     taken from refs. /22,25,26,27,28/.  The Gilbert-Cameron's    9437 1451  157
     composite formula /29/ was used to represent the level       9437 1451  158
     density.  Level density parameters were determined from the  9437 1451  159
     observed s-wave resonance spacing /30/ and the level schemes.9437 1451  160
     the spin cut-off factors in the constant temperature model   9437 1451  161
     were represented by Gruppelaar's prescription /31/.          9437 1451  162
                                                                  9437 1451  163
                  pu-236    pu-237    pu-238    pu-239    pu-240  9437 1451  164
     a   (1/MeV)  25.50      28.00    26.23      29.44    26.96   9437 1451  165
     t     (MeV)   0.442      0.416    0.422      0.398    0.412  9437 1451  166
     c   (1/MeV)   3.06      14.5      2.88      15.0      3.30   9437 1451  167
     E-joint(MeV)  4.71       4.09     4.38       3.97     4.26   9437 1451  168
     sigma**2      8.63       8.18     6.47      11.6      9.69   9437 1451  169
     no. levels    4.0       19.0     22.0       19.0     28.0    9437 1451  170
     E-max (MeV)   0.307      0.4735   1.3103     0.5118   1.2621 9437 1451  171
     D-obs  (eV)   0.395     10.7      0.383      9.0      2.3    9437 1451  172
     Gamma-g(eV)   0.043      0.027    0.043      0.034    0.043  9437 1451  173
                                                                  9437 1451  174
     D-obs of pu-236, -237 and -238 were not available from ref.  9437 1451  175
     /30/, and hence the parameters "a" for these nuclei were     9437 1451  176
     determined assuming its linear dependence on the mass a:     9437 1451  177
         a = 0.365*a - 60.64     for even-even pu isotopes        9437 1451  178
         a = 0.659*a - 128.18    for odd-mass pu isotopes         9437 1451  179
     which were derived by analyzing the data of pu-241, -242,    9437 1451  180
     -243, and -244 as well as pu-239 and -240. Low-lying levels  9437 1451  181
     were hardly observed for pu-236 and it was assumed to be     9437 1451  182
     identical to that of pu-238 to determine the constant        9437 1451  183
     temperature parameters.                                      9437 1451  184
                                                                  9437 1451  185
     Evaluated fission cross section described below was fed to   9437 1451  186
     gnash as a competing process/32/.  The preequilibrium process9437 1451  187
     was taken into account.  Though the parameter f2 was         9437 1451  188
     adjusted, the calculated (n,2n) cross section failed to well 9437 1451  189
     reproduce the measured data.  Therefore, the measured (n,2n) 9437 1451  190
     cross section of Frehaut et al./33/ was adopted in place of  9437 1451  191
     the calculated one.                                          9437 1451  192
