  mt=18                                                           9437 1451  224
     Distributions were calculated with a modified Madland-Nix    9437 1451  225
     model with consideration for multimodal nature of the fission9437 1451  226
     process/39,40/.  The compound nucleus formation cross sec-   9437 1451  227
     tions for fission fragments were calculated using Becchetti- 9437 1451  228
     Greenlees potential/41/.  Up to 3rd-chance-fission were      9437 1451  229
     considered at high incident neutron energies.                9437 1451  230
     A preequilibrium emission was taken into account above 10 MeV9437 1451  231
     as described in Ref./2/. The prefission neutron spectrum     9437 1451  232
     was calculated with the Feshbach-Kerman-Koonin theory /42/.  9437 1451  233
     The Ignatyuk formula/43/ were used to generate the level     9437 1451  234
     density parameters.                                          9437 1451  235
