  mt=16,17,37,91,102  (n,2n),(n,3n),(n,4n),inelastic scattering   9437 1451  269
                       to the continuum, and capture              9437 1451  270
      Data calculated with gnash /23/ were stored under option-1  9437 1451  271
      (multiplicities).  The photon branching data were taken from9437 1451  272
      refs. /22/ and /25,26,27,28/.  Some assumptions were made   9437 1451  273
      for levels of pu-237 and -239 which had no information on   9437 1451  274
      branching: if e1 transitions were allowed to lower levels,  9437 1451  275
      the transition probabilities were equally shared among them.9437 1451  276
      If not, equally shared collective E2 transitions were       9437 1451  277
      assumed.  The photon strength functions were represented by 9437 1451  278
      the Brink-Axel type giant dipole resonance with conventional9437 1451  279
      resonance positions and widths.  They were normalized to    9437 1451  280
      input values at the thermal energy.  The pygmy resonance was9437 1451  281
      introduced only for pu-240.  The parameters were assumed to 9437 1451  282
      be the same as those of u-238 /49/.                         9437 1451  283
