         COMMENTS ON THE 0 KEV TO 1 KEV ENERGY RANGE.             9437 1451  526
***************************************************************** 9437 1451  527
                                                                  9437 1451  528
   AT THE END OF 1987, AN ANALYSIS WAS COMPLETED UP TO 1 KEV. IN A9437 1451  529
PRELIMINARY STEP, A CORRELATED FIT OF HARVEY TRANSMISSION DATA,   9437 1451  530
WESTON 84 FISSION DATA AND BLONS FISSION DATA WAS PERFORMED, WITH 9437 1451  531
POSSIBLE ADJUSTMENT OF THE NORMALIZATION COEFFICIENTS AND OF THE  9437 1451  532
BACKGROUND CORRECTIONS. THIS PRELIMINARY STEP HAS SHOWN THAT THIS 9437 1451  533
ADJUSTMENT WAS NOT NECESSARY TO HAVE CONSISTENCY BETWEEN HARVEY   9437 1451  534
DATA AND WESTON DATA. BLONS DATA NEEDED A LARGE READJUSTMENT OF   9437 1451  535
THE BACKGROUND AND OF THE NORMALIZATION. THEREFORE, THE FINAL FIT 9437 1451  536
WAS PERFORMED ONLY ON HARVEY TRANSMISSION DATA, GWIN 84 FISSION   9437 1451  537
DATA (BELOW 30 EV) AND WESTON 84 FISSION DATA, WITH NO BACKGROUND 9437 1451  538
AND NORMALISATION ADJUSTMENT. BLONS DATA, WHICH HAVE BETTER       9437 1451  539
RESOLUTION THAN WESTON 84 DATA, WERE USED ONLY TO OBTAIN MORE     9437 1451  540
ACCURATE FISSION WIDTHS OF SOME NARROW RESONANCES IN THE HIGH     9437 1451  541
ENERGY RANGE.                                                     9437 1451  542
   IN 1989, PRELIMINARY RESULTS OF THE 1988 WESTON FISSION        9437 1451  543
MEASUREMENT/7/ WERE INCLUDED IN THE SAMMY EXPERIMENTAL DATA       9437 1451  544
BASE.  ONE EXPECTED FROM THIS MEASUREMENT, WHICH WAS PERFORMED BY 9437 1451  545
USING A 86 M FLIGHT PATH WITH A RESOLUTION COMPARABLE TO THE      9437 1451  546
RESOLUTION OF HARVEY TRANSMISSION, A CONFIRMATION OF THE EXCELLENT9437 1451  547
QUALITY OF THE 1984 MEASUREMENT. A CONSISTENT SAMMY FIT OF HARVEY 9437 1451  548
TRANSMISSION, WESTON 84 FISSION AND PRELIMINARY WESTON 88 FISSION 9437 1451  549
WAS RESTARTED FROM THE PARAMETER AND COVARIANCE FILES OBTAINED IN 9437 1451  550
1987.  IT APPEARED THAT LARGE BACKGROUND AND NORMALISATION        9437 1451  551
CORRECTIONS WERE NEEDED ON THE NEW WESTON FISSION TO OBTAIN       9437 1451  552
CONSISTENCY WITH HARVEY TRANSMISSION DATA. THESE CORRECTIONS WERE 9437 1451  553
COMPARABLE TO THOSE FOUND ON BLONS DATA AND WERE NOT UNDERSTOOD BY9437 1451  554
THE AUTHORS OF THE EXPERIMENT. THE LAST SAMMY RUNS WERE PERFORMED 9437 1451  555
BY NOT ALLOWING BACKGROUND AND NORMALIZATION VARIATIONS ON HARVEY 9437 1451  556
TRANSMISSION AND WESTON 84 FISSION(VERY SMALL ERROR BARS WERE     9437 1451  557
ASSIGNED TO THE CORRESPONDING PARAMETERS IN THE COVARIANCE MATRIX)9437 1451  558
AND BY ALLOWING THESE VARIATIONS ON WESTON 88 DATA. A NEW SET OF  9437 1451  559
RESONANCE PARAMETERS WAS OBTAINED,WHICH WAS IMPROVED COMPARED TO  9437 1451  560
THE PREVIOUS SET DUE TO THE VERY HIGH RESOLUTION OF THE NEW WESTON9437 1451  561
FISSION MEASUREMENT.                                              9437 1451  562
   THE CALCULATED AVERAGE FISSION CROSS SECTION IN THE ENERGY     9437 1451  563
RANGE FROM 0.1 KEV TO 1.0 KEV WAS 3.7% SMALLER THAN THE VALUES    9437 1451  564
OBTAINED BY THE ENDF/B-VI STANDARD EVALUATION GROUP, DUE TO THE   9437 1451  565
FACT THAT WESTON 84 DATA WERE 3.1% LOWER THAN THE AVERAGE STANDARD9437 1451  566
VALUE. A NEW MEASUREMENT WAS PERFORMED BY WESTON AND TODD IN 1991 9437 1451  567
/18/ IN ORDER TO CHECK THEIR 1984 DATA. A CAREFUL NORMALIZATION   9437 1451  568
OF THE DATA IN THE THERMAL ENERGY RANGE SHOWED THAT THE 1984 DATA 9437 1451  569
SHOULD BE RENORMALIZED BY ABOUT +3%. TO TAKE INTO ACCOUNT THIS    9437 1451  570
RENORMALIZATION, THE 1989 RESONANCE PARAMETERS WERE MODIFIED AT   9437 1451  571
JAERI/13/ IN THE FOLLOWING WAY:                                   9437 1451  572
   1/ INCREASE OF THE FISSION WIDTH BY 3% AND DECREASE OF THE     9437 1451  573
CAPTURE WIDTH BY A QUANTITY EQUAL TO THE VARIATION OF THE FISSION 9437 1451  574
WIDTH, IN THE NARROW RESONANCES(MAINLY 1+ RESONANCES); THAT DOES  9437 1451  575
NOT MODIFY THE TOTAL CROSS SECTION IN THE CORRESPONDING           9437 1451  576
RESONANCES;                                                       9437 1451  577
   2/ ADJUSTMENT OF THE NEUTRON WIDTH OF THE 0+ RESONANCES BY A   9437 1451  578
REFIT OF THE TRANSMISSION DATA AND OF THE RENORMALIZED WESTON AND 9437 1451  579
TODD 1984 DATA IN ENERGY RANGES WHERE THE CONTRIBUTION OF THE 0+  9437 1451  580
RESONANCES IS DOMINANT, AND INCREASE OF THE OTHER(SMALL) 0+       9437 1451  581
NEUTRON WIDTHS BY 3%. NO SEVERE INCONSISTENCY WAS OBSERVED BETWEEN9437 1451  582
THE TRANSMISSION DATA AND THE NEW FISSION DATA OVER THE DOMINANT  9437 1451  583
0+ RESONANCES;THE DIFFERENCES BETWEEN THE 1989 FITS OF THE TRANS- 9437 1451  584
MISSION AND THE NEW FITS WERE CONSISTENT WITHIN THE EXPERIMENTAL  9437 1451  585
ERROR BARS.                                                       9437 1451  586
