BY T.NAKAGAWA TO THE FACOM 780. THE PRELIMINARY SET OF PARAMETERS 9437 1451  673
OBTAINED AT OAK RIDGE IN 1989 WAS USED AS PRIOR INFORMATIONS TO   9437 1451  674
START THE SAMMY CALCULATIONS. ALSO PRIOR TO THE ANALYSIS, THE CON-9437 1451  675
TRIBUTION OF THE EXTERNAL RESONANCES WAS CALCULATED BY USING THE  9437 1451  676
SET OF THE 0 KEV TO 1 KEV KNOWN RESONANCES, SHIFTED IN THE ENERGY 9437 1451  677
RANGES -1 KEV TO 0 KEV, 2 KEV TO 3KEV AND 3 KEV TO 4 KEV; EQUIVA- 9437 1451  678
LENT CONTRIBUTION WAS OBTAINED BY USING 3 FICTICIOUS RESONANCES   9437 1451  679
BELOW 1 KEV AND 3 FICTICIOUS RESONANCES ABOVE 2 KEV(SEE DETAILS IN9437 1451  680
REF./13/). THE ANALYSIS WAS PERFORMED ON THE THICK AND MEDIUM     9437 1451  681
SAMPLE TRANSMISSIONS OF HARVEY DATA (THE THIN SAMPLE DATA WAS NOT 9437 1451  682
USEFUL IN THE HIGH ENERGY RANGE) AND ON THE 1988 FISSION DATA RE- 9437 1451  683
LEASED BY WESTON AT THE BEGINNING OF 1991/7/. THE DEFINITIVE      9437 1451  684
SAMMY FITS WERE PERFORMED IN APRIL 1992 AFTER RENORMALIZATION OF  9437 1451  685
THE 1988 DATA OF WESTON ON THE ENDF/B-VI STANDARD VALUES BETWEEN 19437 1451  686
KEV AND 2 KEV, IN AGREEMENT WITH THE 1991 NEW MEASUREMENTS OF     9437 1451  687
WESTON AND TODD.                                                  9437 1451  688
