   THE DIFFERENCE OF 1.3% BETWEEN THE AVERAGE CALCULATED TOTAL    9437 1451  723
CROSS SECTION AND THE AVERAGE EXPERIMENTAL CROSS SECTION IN THE   9437 1451  724
ENERGY RANGE FROM 1.0 KEV AND 2.0 KEV IS MAINLY DUE TO THE METHOD 9437 1451  725
OF EVALUATING THE TOTAL CROSS SECTION FROM THE EFFECTIVE CROSS    9437 1451  726
SECTION IN REFERENCE/19/. THE ACCURACY OF THE SAMMY FIT OF THE    9437 1451  727
EXPERIMENTAL TRANSMISSION DATA IS BETTER THAN 0.5% ON THE CROSS   9437 1451  728
SECTION. THE CALCULATED FISSION CROSS SECTIONS ARE IN VERY GOOD   9437 1451  729
AGREEMENT WITH THE EXPERIMENTAL DATA. THE CAPTURE DATA /1/ ARE    9437 1451  730
AVERAGE VALUES OBTAINED FROM THE DATA AVAILABLE IN THE EXFOR FILE 9437 1451  731
AND NORMALIZED TO GWIN 1976 AVERAGE VALUES; THERE ARE LARGE       9437 1451  732
DIFFERENCES BETWEEN THE CALCULATED DATA AND THE EXPERIMENTAL DATA 9437 1451  733
AVERAGED OVER 0.1 KEV INTERVALS; BUT ON THE INTERVAL FROM 1.0 KEV 9437 1451  734
TO 2.0 KEV THE AVERAGE VALUES ARE CONSISTENT WITHIN 1.0%.         9437 1451  735
