   COMMENTS ON THE 2.0 KEV TO 2.5 KEV REGION                      9437 1451  738
***************************************************************** 9437 1451  739
                                                                  9437 1451  740
   THIS ENERGY RANGE WAS ALSO ANALYSED AT JAERI /13/. NO          9437 1451  741
PRELIMINARY SET OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS WAS AVAILABLE PRIOR TO THE9437 1451  742
ANALYSIS. MORE THAN 90% OF THE RESONANCES, COMPARED TO THE LOW    9437 1451  743
ENERGY RANGE, COULD STILL BE IDENTIFIED IN THE TRANSMISSION DATA  9437 1451  744
BETWEEN 2 KEV AND 2.5 KEV. THEREFORE THE CORRELATED SAMMY ANALYSIS9437 1451  745
OF HARVEY TRANSMISSIONS AND WESTON FISSION WAS STILL FEASIBLE IN  9437 1451  746
THIS ENERGY RANGE. THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS OBTAINED ARE          9437 1451  747
CONSISTENT AND HAS NEARLY THE SAME STATISTICAL PROPERTIES AS THOSE9437 1451  748
OF THE RESONANCES IN THE 0 TO 2 KEV ENERGY RANGE. A QUITE GOOD FIT9437 1451  749
OF THE TRANSMISSION AND FISSION DATA WAS OBTAINED WITHOUT         9437 1451  750
BACKGROUND AND NORMALISATION ADJUSTMENT. HOWEVER, THE CALCULATED  9437 1451  751
FISSION CROSS SECTIONS ARE, ON AVERAGE, 1.4% LOWER THAN THE       9437 1451  752
EXPERIMENTAL VALUES.  THIS DIFFERENCE,WHICH HOWEVER IS NOT LARGER 9437 1451  753
THAN THE SYSTEMATIC ERRORS ON THE EXPERIMENTAL DATA, COULD BE DUE 9437 1451  754
TO THE DIFFICULTIES OF IDENTIFYING THE WIDE J=0+ RESONANCES IN THE9437 1451  755
EXPERIMENTAL DATA, BECAUSE THE EFFECTS OF THE INCREASING          9437 1451  756
RESOLUTION AND DOPPLER WIDTHS. PRIOR TO THE SAMMY FITS, THE       9437 1451  757
FISSION DATA OF WESTON AND TODD (1988 HIGH RESOLUTION DATA) WERE  9437 1451  758
NORMALIZED TO THE ENDF/B-VI STANDARD IN THE ENERGY RANGE FROM 1   9437 1451  759
KEV TO 2 KEV.                                                     9437 1451  760
